[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8691"] :question/problem "Find the solution(s) to the equation $2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2 & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =-2 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the solutions to $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-1$ correspond to the values of $x$ at which $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ attains its minimum value.\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-1)=\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\pi $ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\pi .$\n\nThis solution is a quadrantal angle. To find the remaining solutions, we use our knowledge of the cosine function. We know that the cosine function has its minimum values at\n\n$$\nx=\\pi +2n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSince the domain $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi $ is one period, and we have already found one minimum value in this period, we conclude that $x=\\pi $ is the only solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-72841/selection/3ee391c1b541d8f729a14359a46051e188cc67e87f70d0d476fdfa7063f7c44a" :answer/id #uuid "78fa451f-c205-501a-8823-be130e94e18b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72841/selection/bc6c8e1769ccdd266c8226f86de2176b276b827f8fab68b57be0987a8738f4cf" :answer/id #uuid "ee63ea55-8b55-5815-9c45-c118b4c974f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72841/selection/f3ce197c0bf0ff8b852cf7f6b09aed316591849f14268aca6e2ceb70c79bfb8a" :answer/id #uuid "8ee0c786-f018-5427-a547-7884dac6cef8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72841/selection/f7ec98ce0d2d5e0413aaea93f098b04337f2217a14eff2f5b611bfb2fc659059" :answer/id #uuid "ba6741f0-d8a6-59a4-99f5-49c004acd85e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72841/selection/9c2421974ab9da5b645c569d4c4270361bea28563c0e37c29cba78a649ee15ae" :answer/id #uuid "3ca356de-e7d0-5f99-9feb-5d5abb3ca6c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72841/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3c76c249-52f5-53a8-8e1c-50bdf5723b6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72841/selection/f7ec98ce0d2d5e0413aaea93f098b04337f2217a14eff2f5b611bfb2fc659059" :answer-field/choices ["q-72841/selection/3ee391c1b541d8f729a14359a46051e188cc67e87f70d0d476fdfa7063f7c44a" "q-72841/selection/bc6c8e1769ccdd266c8226f86de2176b276b827f8fab68b57be0987a8738f4cf" "q-72841/selection/f3ce197c0bf0ff8b852cf7f6b09aed316591849f14268aca6e2ceb70c79bfb8a" "q-72841/selection/f7ec98ce0d2d5e0413aaea93f098b04337f2217a14eff2f5b611bfb2fc659059" "q-72841/selection/9c2421974ab9da5b645c569d4c4270361bea28563c0e37c29cba78a649ee15ae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72841" :question/id #uuid "39ec17cf-e2ec-5e6d-90c9-4664e7af0135" :question/math-academy-id "q-72841" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{2}{5}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to one decimal place?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{2}{5}) & =1.982\\,313…≈1.982\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $1.982\\,3$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.982\\,3.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R}=\\pi -1.982\\,3 & ≈1.159\\,3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=1.159\\,3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978101/assets/250adbaae0378e3f42ab4340479bb4590aa7f39a1094ea39010de3d5758b4e3e.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +1.159\\,3 \\\\  & ≈4.300\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{x}_{2}≈1.982\\,3\\cdot 4.300\\,9≈8.5\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72841/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f607558-5a7f-52df-b344-57f2f84791e9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72841"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72845/selection/b405a56a7ad5db74f8911431764d391b7bd8cf932f11e81e9e742ae92fbcf21d" :answer/id #uuid "d7373295-9ed5-5bb7-b498-50d1997836c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={60}^{∘},\\,{240}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72845/selection/135ddd24e19ef3138bca0150914abaef384649661c301b69fe1758743889a3ef" :answer/id #uuid "a307f194-28b0-53e7-8807-2bdfb038a57b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={180}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72845/selection/3a42611fb0ffec076b8c9d7a306225c40830435f83a892a8e1231323e05caf6a" :answer/id #uuid "4ab4df43-1a37-5eba-a360-cdf2f27994a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={90}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72845/selection/0916585b83dcd65cbb6acded6997e5eb51f21c14b83a7ad98a1d2db0d126b1f9" :answer/id #uuid "5eee05a2-f6d2-5b71-b692-cacea99c0406" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={30}^{∘},\\,{210}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72845/selection/3daf0487e04cc4c2b369692c65693a0d8b66011a44610fd4eb04aefe8323bff4" :answer/id #uuid "366b45b0-33d6-5d4b-a203-1f162a1b3985" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={0}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72845/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2abec0f8-c293-5a1e-b660-9e22a95b2bab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72845/selection/135ddd24e19ef3138bca0150914abaef384649661c301b69fe1758743889a3ef" :answer-field/choices ["q-72845/selection/b405a56a7ad5db74f8911431764d391b7bd8cf932f11e81e9e742ae92fbcf21d" "q-72845/selection/135ddd24e19ef3138bca0150914abaef384649661c301b69fe1758743889a3ef" "q-72845/selection/3a42611fb0ffec076b8c9d7a306225c40830435f83a892a8e1231323e05caf6a" "q-72845/selection/0916585b83dcd65cbb6acded6997e5eb51f21c14b83a7ad98a1d2db0d126b1f9" "q-72845/selection/3daf0487e04cc4c2b369692c65693a0d8b66011a44610fd4eb04aefe8323bff4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72845" :question/id #uuid "c6affe1a-b4aa-5c33-add9-f7ef175f8a68" :question/math-academy-id "q-72845" :question/problem "Find the solution(s) to the equation $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3}{2}=1$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3 & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the solutions to $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1$ correspond to the values of $x$ at which $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ attains its minimum value.\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-1)={180}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${180}^{∘}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={180}^{∘}.$\n\nThis solution is a quadrantal angle. To find the remaining solutions, we use our knowledge of the cosine function. We know that the cosine function has its minimum values at\n\n$$\nx={180}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\n$$\n\nSince the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}$ is one period, and we have already found one minimum value in this period, we conclude that $x={180}^{∘}$ is the only solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-72845/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9f482ac-9771-52a3-9517-8494c3de6379"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72845"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120989/selection/996b3bf2ac1d086ab99a2993d4e2963c350df2485a96b21f25839638028cd262" :answer/id #uuid "07f2daad-1f76-5441-b88b-f86f790f010e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-560" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120989/selection/e5b57c0c9b30c9b652d86e7f88de30dcbbb1c40cbf667f193858d2c51c4e7916" :answer/id #uuid "aa0dc536-a707-54b6-923b-b6584bf5ea7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-650" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120989/selection/1fd9da084030c02fca966c3beda38546035a9dc62aa82e38fbe3786fb6941e44" :answer/id #uuid "89356a7b-59fa-5f75-96c2-e2cbd1787120" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-610" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120989/selection/6aa68cd9eb0195bcaddfb3acfc1dd55e5ce6f1d998586fc6cbe8559f8febc296" :answer/id #uuid "a7c5042b-37f9-5757-b786-97efa1e97499" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-670" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120989/selection/f81e4ab27cbdf203879234e5b66bd1245262bdb1eeb53d4f0944cfd64dc49a54" :answer/id #uuid "b89f984c-b009-5a3a-9a8f-e7b38e7cbfc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-590" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120989/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "441dceb6-7ee1-54a3-b35a-6ef51a6df2e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120989/selection/6aa68cd9eb0195bcaddfb3acfc1dd55e5ce6f1d998586fc6cbe8559f8febc296" :answer-field/choices ["q-120989/selection/996b3bf2ac1d086ab99a2993d4e2963c350df2485a96b21f25839638028cd262" "q-120989/selection/e5b57c0c9b30c9b652d86e7f88de30dcbbb1c40cbf667f193858d2c51c4e7916" "q-120989/selection/1fd9da084030c02fca966c3beda38546035a9dc62aa82e38fbe3786fb6941e44" "q-120989/selection/6aa68cd9eb0195bcaddfb3acfc1dd55e5ce6f1d998586fc6cbe8559f8febc296" "q-120989/selection/f81e4ab27cbdf203879234e5b66bd1245262bdb1eeb53d4f0944cfd64dc49a54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120989" :question/id #uuid "c7c27ee1-3dad-5834-b592-aad9797bac23" :question/math-academy-id "q-120989" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0.9$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest ten?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(0.9)=25.841\\,932{…}^{∘}≈{25.84}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${25.84}^{∘}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={25.84}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of \n${\\theta }_{R}={25.84}^{∘}.$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fourth quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={25.84}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978101/assets/4c65ecb4fdcefc332b75f2b459f65ba872a2d2d0826b27ba80df1c8f8f3b606e.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $4$th quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={360}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}-{25.84}^{∘} \\\\  & ={334.16}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get a second solution that's within the required domain, we simply subtract ${360}^{∘}$ from $X:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =X-{360}^{∘} \\\\  & ={334.16}^{∘}-{360}^{∘} \\\\  & =-{25.84}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=25.84\\cdot (-25.84)≈-670\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest ten." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120989/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26666440-d376-5cb6-b922-9850e5c42eb3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120989"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338573/field-1/1410c9af32d8d87e684df0411ab0e7722636fa1ec5619bab95820e4c8b61b93b" :answer/id #uuid "828955d0-4bdc-5c49-b12f-6ce3cc3d47db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-135" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338573/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "519ecf6b-bba2-55bf-9017-4fb1b4847e58" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338573/field-1/1410c9af32d8d87e684df0411ab0e7722636fa1ec5619bab95820e4c8b61b93b" :answer-field/choices ["q-338573/field-1/1410c9af32d8d87e684df0411ab0e7722636fa1ec5619bab95820e4c8b61b93b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338573/field-2/c89a78e01f135d27857f87b29786d3bde75753fd31e9ec00c0c39b58d64c0b12" :answer/id #uuid "96767617-dbb2-5ccc-bfcb-1e0de7d8bcfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "135" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338573/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "621ad334-5a88-5156-8f3d-75e59356fa70" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338573/field-2/c89a78e01f135d27857f87b29786d3bde75753fd31e9ec00c0c39b58d64c0b12" :answer-field/choices ["q-338573/field-2/c89a78e01f135d27857f87b29786d3bde75753fd31e9ec00c0c39b58d64c0b12"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338573" :question/id #uuid "bd69c5c8-719b-532b-8d1c-6d7b04b275f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-338573" :question/problem "Arranged in **ascending order**, the solutions of the equation $8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4\\sqrt{2}=0$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}$ are $x=${{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4\\sqrt{2} & =0 \\\\ 8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =-4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})={135}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${135}^{∘}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is $x={135}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978101/assets/91e4de557177693203cbbc48c12bbf7af3de1739c8405ac05bdfa06d3e92638c.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{45}^{∘} \\\\  & ={225}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get a second solution that's within the required domain, we simply subtract ${360}^{∘}$ from $X:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =X-{360}^{∘} \\\\  & ={225}^{∘}-{360}^{∘} \\\\  & =-{135}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, arranged in ascending order, the solutions are $x={-135}^{∘}$ and $x={135}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-338573/field-1" "q-338573/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26666440-d376-5cb6-b922-9850e5c42eb3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338573"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
